{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run2:inflation:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:16d2a0b60e717820fdcc80d104cce72762006d70832491083c0d0f0114cd6360","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"categorical","probabilities":{"A":0.15,"B":0.5,"C":0.22,"D":0.13}},"questionHash":"sha256:ca2a4311940635fba34c40e7278721deb2f4716732e6011c94e6eb0554263e61","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq6","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"Lexical-priority lock applied, first match wins, against MY OWN CQ3 (0.90 / 1.75 / 2.80, two-piece normal, sigma_left 0.66, sigma_right 0.82) and MY OWN OECD-38 GDP-weighted core path from CQ2 (2027-2036 average 2.65%, front-loaded 2.85% then 2.47%, so the 2032-36 central is 2.45% with sigma ~0.40 on a five-year average). P(core 2032-36 >= 2.70%) = 1 - Phi(0.625) = 0.27. P(core 2032-36 < 2.00%) = Phi(-1.125) = 0.13.\nSTEP 1, A (growth >= 2.6%/yr): 1 - Phi((2.60-1.75)/0.82) = 1 - Phi(1.037) = 0.150 -> A = 15. PINNED to my own CQ3 right tail, not chosen. My P50 of 1.75% forbids most mass on A and does not get it. A sits just below the standalone AI-Q6 Transformative Breakout at 16.2%, which is coherent: coupled A can be reached by China upside without any TFP breakout, and is made harder by the locked aging drag being endogenous.\nSTEP 2, C (OECD-38 core >= 2.70% AND growth < 2.0%): P(growth < 2.0) = 0.620. P(core >= 2.70) = 0.27. Stagflation correlation +0.25 (a supply-wall regime is both hot and slow). 0.620x0.27 + 0.25xsqrt(0.62x0.38x0.27x0.73) = 0.1674 + 0.25x0.2155 = 0.221 -> C = 22. Disjoint from A on growth (>=2.6 vs <2.0), no overlap correction.\nSTEP 3, D (growth < 1.7% AND core < 2.00%): P(growth < 1.7) = Phi((1.70-1.75)/0.66) = 0.470. P(core < 2.00) = 0.13 — the sharpest disagreement in my payload against the Wave-1 centre of 0.25-0.30, and it is NOT a view about AI's deflationary power. Getting the OECD-38 aggregate under 2.00% is a three-way conjunction: the five high-inflation members at a 7-11% weight must disinflate to ~3%, AND shelter must go under 2% against a demographic channel that raises households per capita, AND the counter-cyclically imputed financial-services lines must turn negative. Correlation +0.40 (one demand-deficit cause produces low growth and low inflation jointly). 0.470x0.13 + 0.40xsqrt(0.47x0.53x0.13x0.87) = 0.0611 + 0.40x0.1678 = 0.128 -> D = 13. I also respect the Historian's hard constraint that no 5-year window of OECD+China PPP growth since 1960 has printed below 1.7%, even 2008-2012 at ~2.4%, and I kill D on the INFLATION leg rather than fudging my own growth distribution.\nSTEP 4, B = residual = 100 - 15 - 22 - 13 = 50. Sum = 100 exactly. B is also where my lens independently wants the mass: electricity, construction and care at 4-6% against genuinely market-priced software, media and tradable goods at 0-1% nets, at core weights, to a 2.0-2.69% aggregate — neither C's >=2.70% nor D's <2.00%. Extreme relative-price SKEW with a moderately-above-target LEVEL is the barbell.\nCONSISTENCY CHECK AGAINST MY OWN CQ3, PERFORMED: A = 15 is read off the fitted right tail of 0.90/1.75/2.80 rather than set independently; the P50 of 1.75% falls squarely inside B's residual cell (growth 1.7-2.5% with core between 2.00 and 2.69%), which is why B is the largest single cell; D's growth leg is P(growth<1.7) = 0.470 straight off my own left tail.\nCONSISTENCY CHECK AGAINST MY OWN CQ2, PERFORMED: CQ2 = 32 is the JOINT of (core >= 2.50% over 2027-2036, marginal 0.64) and (China CPI < 1.50%, marginal 0.47). CQ6-C is a DIFFERENT event — a higher bar (2.70%) over a later, shorter window (2032-36), carrying no China condition. Dropping the China conjunct raises it; the higher bar and the back-half window lower it; and P(core >= 2.50%, 2027-36) = 0.64 against P(core >= 2.70%, 2032-36) = 0.27 is mutually consistent ONLY because of the front-loaded path (2.85% then 2.47%). THIS IS THE SINGLE INTERNAL JOINT ON WHICH MY CQ6 PIVOTS, the same pivot Fermi and the Bayesian both identified: if the path were FLAT at my 10-year average of 2.65%, P(>=2.70% in 2032-36) would be ~0.42 and C would rise to ~32 with B falling to ~40. B + C = 72, comfortably above CQ2's 32, so the hot-OECD cell is not oversubscribed; D = 13 is the amount of deflationary mass a 0.64 conjunct-A can carry.\nCOHERENCE WITH CQ4 AND CQ5, PERFORMED: r - g = 2.20 - 1.75 = +0.45pp, so debt/GDP does not stabilize through the denominator, which independently caps A and matches B's \"steep real term premia\" language; and CQ5 at 27 requires the non-rallying (C-type) crash to be more probable than the bond-rallying (D-type) one, which my C = 22 > D = 13 delivers.\nWHERE I LAND RELATIVE TO THE PANEL: 15/50/22/13 against Historian 17/53/13/17, Fermi 9/45/24/22, Scout 17/42/21/20, Bayesian 13/53/22/12, Red-Teamer 25/39/26/10. I am near the Bayesian on A/B/C but I reach C = 22 by a different route (basket construction plus the EM weight, where he had only the EM weight) and I keep D at 13 rather than the Red-Teamer's 10 because his central core of 2.88% stacks three one-directional corrections.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:57.409Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"Turkiye annual CPI (TurkStat, December print) averages below 8.0%/yr over calendar 2028-2031 AND Mexico's headline CPI (INEGI) averages below 3.5% over the same four years. Both required, so a single good Turkish year does not trigger it.\",\"by_when\":\"Feb 28, 2032 (full-year 2031 releases)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the single load-bearing term in my CQ2: the five high-inflation OECD-38 members contributing ~0.70pp to GDP-weighted core. That contribution would fall toward ~0.40pp and my 2027-2036 aggregate from 2.65% to ~2.35%. CQ2 conjunct A falls from 0.64 to ~0.42 and CQ2 from 32 to ~21; CQ6-C falls from 22 to ~16 and CQ6-D rises from 13 to ~18, with B absorbing the balance; CQ4 P50 falls ~0.15pp to ~2.05; hypothesis plank (c) rises from 45 to ~58. My whole divergence from the Historian's CQ2 of 14 would stand revealed as a weighting convention rather than a finding.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"BLS PPI for software publishers AND for computer systems design, plus the euro-area HICP professional-services sub-indices, show OUTRIGHT annual declines of 1.0% or more for two consecutive years in those market-priced (not cost- or asset-fee-imputed) series.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the half of the Red-Teamer's imputation attack that I accepted — that the genuinely deflatable slice of core is only 0.08-0.12 rather than 0.20-0.25 and is partly counter-cyclically hot. My 2032-36 core central falls from 2.45% to ~2.25%, taking P(core >= 2.70%) from 0.27 to ~0.14: CQ6-C falls from 22 to ~14, B rises to ~56, D rises to ~15, A unchanged at 15; CQ2 falls to ~25. The Wave-1 unanimous 'extreme skew, dull aggregate' thesis would be vindicated against both me and the Red Team, and he would be the effort's worst input rather than its best corrective.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China headline CPI (NBS), three-year average over calendar 2031-2033, exceeds 2.2%/yr, with the services sub-index above the goods sub-index in at least two of those three years. My split-window build is 2027-2030 at ~1.0% and 2031-2036 at ~1.9-2.1%, giving a decade average knife-edge against the 1.50% bar.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31, 2034\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Collapses CQ2's China conjunct from 0.47 to ~0.18, taking CQ2 from 32 to ~17. It also means the Chinese labour-scarcity services-wage channel turned reflationary earlier than the locked 2A arithmetic implies, which raises China's growth leg: CQ3 P50 rises ~0.10pp to ~1.85 and P10 to ~1.0, CQ6-D falls ~3 to 10 and A rises ~2 to 17. The services-above-goods condition is there so that a hog cycle or an oil shock alone does not fire it.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Count of OECD-38 members that enact a binding national or sector-wide care-wage award worth 5% or more in real terms, cumulatively over 2027-2031 (tracked in OECD Health at a Glance and national LTC reimbursement schedules), reaches six or more — against zero or one as the null.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"This is the cheapest available test of the mechanism on which I overrode the Bayesian Updater's CQ1 of 8, namely that administered care prices move in discrete statutory level jumps rather than never. Six or more awards takes CQ1's second conjunct from 0.22 to ~0.33 and CQ1 from 16 to ~24, raises plank (a) from 6 to ~12, and adds ~0.08pp to my core path via the ISIC Q channel (CQ2 to ~34, CQ6-C to ~24). Zero or one takes conjunct B to ~0.12 and CQ1 to ~10, i.e. all the way back to the Wave-1 centre, and vindicates the pure fiscal-quantity-rationing read.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"ICE BofA MOVE calendar-year average stays below 85 in every year 2027-2031 while the G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yield averages above 4.0% across the same five years. Both required: a low-vol, high-rate regime is the configuration that kills the level-scaling term.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the baseline assumption behind my CQ5 conjunct A of 0.37 — that a ~85-95 structural baseline plus one 12-18 month crisis clears a decade mean of 105 — and vindicates the Scout's reading that the 2026 compression at 64-71 with nominals already at 3-4% is structural rather than policy-certainty-driven. CQ5 falls from 27 to ~15; CQ4 P90 falls from 3.80 to ~3.30 and P50 to ~2.05 as the term-premium add is shown to be unwarranted; CQ6-C falls ~4 to 18 with B absorbing it. The reverse — MOVE averaging above 110 in both 2029 and 2030 — takes CQ5 to ~38 and CQ4 P50 to ~2.50.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'inflation'."}}